# Kept deliberately short. Every extra exclusion is a chance to remove something the server turns
# out to read at runtime. These entries matter for a local `docker build` and as an explicit
# statement of what must never reach an image.

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci`. Copying a host node_modules in would shadow that with
# whatever architecture the host happens to be.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# THE DATABASE. server/.data is the local PGlite directory. Baking a local database into an image
# is the worst thing on this list.
server/.data*

# Prompt-diff baselines. They render real card titles from real meetings, so they are real meeting
# content and have no business in an image.
server/.fixtures

# Secrets. The host injects real values as environment variables; a committed or local .env must
# never win over them, and must never be readable from a layer.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.gitignore
*.log
